│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_rank_annealing                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the uniformly random configuration with a deterministic multi-start local search  │
│                          │ specialized for the maximin triangle objective. Four points are fixed at the corners of   │
│                          │ the unit square, making the convex hull area exactly one and preventing normalization     │
│                          │ changes from obscuring progress. The remaining nine points begin from perturbed 3-by-3    │
│                          │ lattice layouts and are refined using vectorized evaluation of all 286 triangle areas.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses a rank-weighted objective concentrated on the smallest triangle areas     │
│                          │ rather than only the single current bottleneck. This is substantially more stable than    │
│                          │ direct random sampling: it lifts several nearly-degenerate triangles simultaneously while │
│                          │ retaining the true minimum-area incumbent. Fixed seeds, fixed restart count, and fixed    │
│                          │ proposal schedule make the returned arrangement reproducible.                             │
