│ patch_description        │ Replace the single perturbed-grid initialization with a deterministic family of           │
│                          │ lattice-based seeds at several perturbation scales. This gives the maximin search many    │
│                          │ initially well-spaced configurations while avoiding the exact collinearities that make a  │
│                          │ regular grid unusable.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also replace the fixed, overly aggressive differential scale with a cooling               │
│                          │ differential-evolution proposal and an attraction toward the incumbent best               │
│                          │ configuration. A scale of 0.78 frequently clips points onto square edges and destroys     │
│                          │ promising triangle constraints; decreasing the scale over generations yields large        │
│                          │ basin-changing moves early and useful geometric refinements later.                        │
