│ patch_description        │ This replaces slow single-point simulated annealing with a compact 3-fold-symmetric       │
│                          │ parameterization searched by vectorized differential evolution. The convex region is a    │
│                          │ fixed unit-scale equilateral triangle, with three hull vertices, one center point, and    │
│                          │ three independently rotated rings of three points each. This reduces the optimization     │
│                          │ from 18 free coordinates to only six meaningful geometric variables: three ring radii and │
│                          │ three phase offsets.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The resulting population search evaluates hundreds of candidate layouts simultaneously    │
│                          │ using NumPy, avoids expensive scalar triangle evaluation loops, guarantees every point    │
│                          │ remains inside the convex hull, and uses deterministic restarts plus a final batch local  │
│                          │ polish. The equilateral hull is especially compatible with triangle-area maximization and │
│                          │ the imposed rotational structure avoids the grid-like collinear triples that harmed       │
│                          │ earlier implementations.                                                                  │
