╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hexagonal_orbit_de                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces unrestricted 18-dimensional point mutation with a            │
│                          │ symmetry-reduced differential-evolution search over a structured 3-fold rotational        │
│                          │ family. The configuration consists of a center point, two optimized interior 3-point      │
│                          │ rotational orbits, and two fixed outer rotational orbits forming a regular hexagonal      │
│                          │ hull.                                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The regular hexagon guarantees a known convex hull and avoids the restrictive             │
│                          │ corner-triangle bottlenecks imposed by a square. Only four continuous parameters are      │
│                          │ optimized: two orbit radii and two orbit phases. This substantially reduces the search    │
│                          │ space while retaining non-grid, non-collinear configurations. A deterministic population  │
