│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_fixedhull13                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The previous approach used a 160-member differential-evolution population for 360         │
│                          │ generations, optimized a lower-tail surrogate over freely moving square points, and then  │
│                          │ applied 2,200 single-point local moves to six finalists. Its main weakness is that many   │
│                          │ global-search candidates have a hull substantially smaller than the unit square, so raw   │
│                          │ triangle-area optimization does not consistently optimize the normalized evaluation       │
│                          │ metric.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version fixes the four unit-square corners, making the convex hull area exactly one  │
│                          │ for every candidate. It uses a larger 192-member population, 460 current-to-elite         │
│                          │ differential-evolution generations, a stronger early mutation range (0.82 to 0.48), and a │
│                          │ 20-triangle lower-tail surrogate. The polish phase uses batches of                        │
│                          │ active-constraint-targeted proposals: points participating in the smallest 14 triangles   │
│                          │ are selected preferentially, with occasional two-point mutations. This directs local      │
│                          │ evaluations toward the triangles controlling the true minimum area while retaining        │
│                          │ deterministic seeded behavior.                                                            │
