│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the square-constrained search with a triangular convex hull, which  │
│                          │ is more compatible with the known geometry of strong Heilbronn-type configurations. It    │
│                          │ uses a deterministic 3-fold-symmetric differential-evolution stage to efficiently locate  │
│                          │ high-quality global arrangements, followed by an unconstrained sparse local polish of the │
│                          │ ten non-hull points.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hull is an equilateral triangle rescaled to have exactly unit area, so the minimum    │
│                          │ raw triangle area equals the normalized objective. The differential-evolution population  │
│                          │ includes periodic diversity replacement, preventing premature collapse into nearly        │
│                          │ identical layouts. All random choices use a fixed seed and all candidate points are       │
│                          │ projected back into the triangular region.                                                │
