│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fixed_hull_maximin                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Exploit affine invariance by fixing the convex hull to the unit square for every          │
│                          │ candidate, not merely a minority of initial candidates. This makes the raw triangle area  │
│                          │ exactly equal to the normalized objective throughout differential evolution, removing the │
│                          │ major objective mismatch caused by variable hull areas. It also reduces the search        │
│                          │ dimension from 26 to 18 free coordinates and prevents the optimizer from spending effort  │
│                          │ perturbing hull corners. The lower-tail term is reduced so selection more directly        │
│                          │ maximizes the required worst-triangle criterion.                                          │
