│ patch_description        │ The prior program uses a six-parameter 3-fold ring family with a 300-member               │
│                          │ differential-evolution population, 570 generations, soft-min finite-difference            │
│                          │ refinement, and sparse random polish. Its main limitation is that final refinement        │
│                          │ distributes effort uniformly across all ring parameters even though only a small subset   │
│                          │ of rings typically participates in the currently limiting triangles.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version retains the unit-area equilateral hull and deterministic six-parameter       │
│                          │ representation, but changes the optimization schedule: a larger structured/global         │
│                          │ population uses a mixed DE/current-to-elite portfolio, followed by an active-constraint   │
│                          │ bottleneck polish. During polish, the smallest triangle constraints are inspected         │
│                          │ directly; ring parameters are selected proportionally to their participation in those     │
│                          │ constraints. The local search includes coordinated radius/phase moves and paired-ring     │
│                          │ perturbations, while accepting only strict improvements to the exact minimum triangle     │
│                          │ area. This focuses the fixed evaluation budget on dimensions controlling the active       │
│                          │ bottlenecks and removes the relatively expensive finite-difference soft-min gradient      │
│                          │ stage.                                                                                    │
