│ patch_description        │ The current program uses four expensive 45,000-step simulated-annealing restarts over 18  │
│                          │ free square-interior coordinates, with a decaying tail blend from 0.09 to 0 and           │
│                          │ coordinate pattern search. Its strongest limitation is the high-dimensional square        │
│                          │ parameterization: four fixed corners create restrictive boundary triangles, while random  │
│                          │ single-point moves spend most evaluations outside useful maximin basins.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement uses a unit-area equilateral hull and a compact symmetry-aware           │
│                          │ six-parameter family: the three hull vertices, centroid, and three independently phased   │
│                          │ 3-fold rings. The hull has exact area one, and ring radii are restricted to the inscribed │
│                          │ disk, guaranteeing containment. A deterministic Latin-hypercube population is optimized   │
│                          │ with a differential-evolution portfolio. It uses stronger early lower-tail protection     │
│                          │ (`0.12`, smallest 18 triangles), decaying to exact maximin selection, periodic diversity  │
│                          │ refreshes, and final adaptive sparse local polishing. This reduces search dimension from  │
│                          │ 18 to 6 while exploring substantially more globally distinct configurations per           │
│                          │ evaluation budget.                                                                        │
