│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single current-to-best DE donor rule (`population +            │
│                          │ attraction*(best-population) + factor*(a-b)`) with population 384, 720 generations, two   │
│                          │ 20% restarts, and 260 batch-polish rounds. This can converge prematurely because every    │
│                          │ member is increasingly pulled toward the same phase-locked basin.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The revised implementation retains the efficient six-parameter 3-ring construction and    │
│                          │ guaranteed unit-area triangular hull, but replaces the single donor strategy with a       │
│                          │ deterministic progress-scheduled mutation portfolio: broad `rand/1` donors dominate early │
│                          │ exploration, current-to-elite donors become more frequent during exploitation, and        │
│                          │ elite-difference donors supply late basin refinement. Selection uses a lower-tail merit   │
│                          │ early in the run, improving several near-active triangle constraints rather than only the │
│                          │ single current minimum. Final polishing is active-constraint weighted, preferentially     │
│                          │ perturbing rings participating in small triangles.                                        │
