│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ triangular_hull_schedule                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Constrain every evolutionary candidate to a common triangular hull with vertices `(0,0)`, │
│                          │ `(1,0)`, and `(0,1)`. This is particularly appropriate for the affine-invariant           │
│                          │ objective: the hull area is fixed at `1/2`, so raw triangle-area ranking is exactly       │
│                          │ proportional to normalized ranking. It also removes arbitrary hull variation, preserves   │
│                          │ the classical three-fold/triangular Heilbronn geometry bias, and makes every DE           │
│                          │ generation optimize a consistent objective.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The former population mixed square-hull, variable-hull, and anchored candidates, so its   │
│                          │ fast DE score was often not aligned with the evaluated normalized score. The replacement  │
│                          │ uses folded stratified samples in the fixed simplex. It also changes the tail objective   │
│                          │ from strong early lower-tail protection to nearly exact maximin selection late in DE,     │
│                          │ then prevents polishing from moving the three hull vertices.                              │
│ num_applied              │ 5                                                                                         │
