│ patch_name               │ coordinate_active_polish                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic coordinate-pattern refinement after the stochastic polish. The        │
│                          │ maximin objective is piecewise linear in each point position between changes of the       │
│                          │ active limiting triangle, so testing the six barycentric tangent directions for every     │
│                          │ free point is substantially more reliable than relying only on random final               │
│                          │ perturbations. All moves preserve barycentric sum before projection, retain strict        │
│                          │ containment in the fixed equilateral hull, and are accepted only on a true                │
│                          │ minimum-determinant improvement. The coarse-to-fine schedule can resolve residual         │
│                          │ active-set defects while adding only small batched evaluations.                           │
