│ patch_description        │ Fix a correctness issue in the annealing loop: the previous code could update             │
│                          │ `best_points` using a rejected proposal after restoring `points`, causing `best_minimum`  │
│                          │ and the returned configuration to become inconsistent. This can prevent the final strict  │
│                          │ polishing stage from accepting valid improvements because it compares against an          │
│                          │ unattainable recorded score.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, bias a portion of annealing proposals toward points participating in the    │
│                          │ current low-area active set and introduce occasional coupled two-point moves. Heilbronn   │
│                          │ optima are usually controlled by networks of simultaneously tight triangles, so moving    │
│                          │ only uniformly selected individual points makes it difficult to escape arrangements where │
│                          │ two active constraints must be relieved together. The exact primary minimum remains the   │
│                          │ criterion for global-best preservation.                                                   │
