│ patch_description        │ This hybrid retains the efficient threefold-symmetric equilateral-triangle construction   │
│                          │ from the current program, while incorporating the lower-tail stabilization and elitist    │
│                          │ differential-evolution ideas from the square-based implementation.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search fixes the convex hull to an equilateral triangle, which is subsequently scaled │
│                          │ to unit area. Therefore raw triangle area is exactly the requested normalized objective   │
│                          │ after scaling. Differential evolution uses a score dominated by the minimum triangle area │
│                          │ but augmented by the mean of the twelve smallest areas, reducing fragile one-constraint   │
│                          │ solutions. Several finalists are then independently polished with projected               │
│                          │ sparse-coordinate perturbations, permitting controlled symmetry breaking while preserving │
│                          │ feasibility inside the convex hull. All random behavior uses one fixed seed.              │
