│ patch_name               │ coordinate_poll_refinement                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace part of the purely stochastic sparse polishing batch with a deterministic         │
│                          │ coordinate-pattern poll over every non-hull point. Maximin triangle objectives are        │
│                          │ piecewise linear and nonsmooth: near a good configuration, random multi-point moves       │
│                          │ frequently damage one of the active minimum-area triangles before finding an improving    │
│                          │ direction. Explicit positive/negative x/y polls for each of the ten movable points        │
│                          │ provide a reliable local direct-search mechanism, while the remaining candidates retain   │
│                          │ random multi-point perturbations for diagonal and basin-changing moves. This preserves    │
│                          │ determinism, convex feasibility through the existing barycentric projection, and adds no  │
│                          │ expensive objective evaluations because the batch size is unchanged.                      │
