│ patch_name               │ batch_active_de13                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses six sequential simulated-annealing restarts of 36,000           │
│                          │ proposals, with an initial step of 0.112, lower-tail blend weight 0.085, temperature      │
│                          │ 0.0025, and a 10-scale bottleneck polish beginning at 0.018. Its main limitation is that  │
│                          │ most proposals modify only one point and are evaluated serially, making basin exploration │
│                          │ relatively narrow.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version replaces the long sequential annealing schedule with a vectorized population │
│                          │ search. It uses 104 concurrent layouts, 980 generations, three complementary proposal     │
│                          │ types per generation (correlated local perturbation, differential-evolution transport,    │
│                          │ and bottleneck-targeted moves), periodic diversity injection, and a lower-tail surrogate  │
│                          │ that decays from 0.070 to zero. The final stage is strict maximin-only active-set         │
│                          │ polishing with coordinated one- and two-point proposals. All layouts remain inside a unit │
│                          │ square with fixed corners, so the raw minimum triangle area remains exactly the           │
│                          │ hull-normalized objective.                                                                │
