│                          │ annealed lower-tail objective from the simplex implementation. Four fixed square corners  │
│                          │ guarantee a unit convex hull, making raw triangle area exactly equal to the normalized    │
│                          │ objective and avoiding repeated hull computation during optimization.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation uses stratified, random, and center-biased starts; a vectorized hybrid │
│                          │ differential-evolution phase; annealed tail protection; and batched active-triangle local │
│                          │ refinement. Local refinement preferentially moves points participating in the currently   │
│                          │ smallest triangles, which is substantially more effective than uniformly selecting        │
